  "id": "COMPOUND:21079 - PROTEIN:4936",
  "verbalization": "Palmarumycin CP18 is implicated in the biological pathway leading to Lu1 through multiple indirect mechanisms. The drug is directly linked to MC116, which is a target of Oxytroflavoside G, and subsequently, 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which also targets Lu1. This suggests a potential role for palmarumycin CP18 in modulating the activity of these compounds, possibly through the regulation of their targets. Additionally, palmarumycin CP18 is associated with TE-11, which is also a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, further reinforcing the chain of interaction. The evidence indicates that palmarumycin CP18 may influence the downstream signaling pathways involving these compounds, ultimately affecting Lu1. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which palmarumycin CP18 could exert its biological effects, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
